WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
"Welcome"

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.950
I don't know why we have to be in such a hurry.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.200
You're late!

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.580
Jeez. Our club sure is full of impatient people.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.250
I swear, our president is so unreliable.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.620
Well, at least they're here in time.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.200
The train's here!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.370
Please stay behind the yellow line.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.790
These seats work, right?

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.910
Want a Shiranui orange?

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.040
Oh, I'll take one. Thanks.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.040
Were you late because you were buying those?

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.950
Bingo!

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.950
Perfect snack for the train, don't ya think?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.500
Yeah, I guess.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.910
It's so sweet!

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.700
The next stop is Yamanoura, Yamanoura.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.540
Please make sure that you have all of your
belongings before you get off the train.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.500
We're all going shopping today!

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.790
Thanks for the meal.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.500
The flatheads were so good!

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.910
Guess it's time to clean up.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:26.910
Okay.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.620
President Kuroiwa, thanks for letting
me use your hat again today.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.950
No probs.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.750
Ya don't have yer own hat, Tsurugi?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.370
I don't...

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.290
Since I didn't go out much.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.120
That probably means you
don't have a Jacke either.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.580
Jacke? What's that?

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.290
You two! Help me clean up already!

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.700
This is a Jacke! Rain resistant,
wind resistant, wave-splash resistant!

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.200
It's basically super convenient.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.500
Ah... Yeah, I don't have
anything outdoorsy like that.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.080
Well, ya need to get one.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.330
But...

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.830
What's up?

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.500
That one's a bit... you know?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.500
Yeah.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.950
What?

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.500
No high school girl would
be caught dead in that!

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.910
I mean, maybe if it was cuter...

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:31.200
What are ya talkin' about? Jackes are awesome!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.160
You need to be a little more fashionable, Sis.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.330
Y'all can call me behind the times all ya want.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.580
But also call me "President!"

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.910
There are some cute ones, too.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:47.330
There's a fishing shop that sells clothes
and supplies geared towards girls.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.370
Oh, really?

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.000
That really big fishing shop, right?

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.330
I think you'll find something
you like there, Hina.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.160
Really?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.120
Well, let's all go there tomorrow.
I have stuff I wanna look for, too.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.700
Let's go!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.660
All right. We'll meet at the train station
after school tomorrow.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.080
Okay!

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.080
I hope I can find a cute one.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.830
Say, Hina.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.540
You good on funds?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.000
Yeah. I brought 10,000 yen just in case.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.250
I had to ask for an advance on my allowance.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.410
That should be plenty.
You'll definitely get some change.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.250
All right, let's get something to eat
on the way back. Hina's treat!

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.620
W-Wait, why me?

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.830
I want a chocolate parfait!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.120
No way.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.790
I want some <i>ikinari dango</i>.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.700
Mont Blanc, please.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:46.410
Don't encourage her, you two!

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.120
We're here.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.040
I thought a fishing supply store
would be a lot smaller.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.870
Well, this is the biggest shop in the area.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:10.870
Hina, over here!
They have a lot of fishing apparel!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.160
Wow... I hope I can find a cute one.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.790
I-I-It's not cute...

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.620
These are for men.
They'll have what you're looking for upstairs.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.620
Huh?

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.080
My bad. I jumped the gun.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.330
Jeez, you scared me.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.910
Wow, this is so cute!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:46.330
Nice. This one's adorable!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.370
Which one do you like, Natsumi?

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.040
Let's see. For me, personally...

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.700
I'd go for this one...

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.410
...or maybe this one.

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.500
Why are you posing like that?

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.700
Posing like a gravure model.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.870
You're so weird.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.370
Oh, shut up.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.200
This one's really cute.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.120
Yeah.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.370
You should try some on, too, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.540
Well, I'm pretty big
so I can never find my size.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.120
Though I'd love to wear something like this.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.700
Right... I guess that might
be an issue when they're big.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.080
The two of us might never
have to worry about that.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.620
I-I was talking about my height...

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.040
I wish I could relate...

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.580
Tsurugi.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.080
Come here.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.120
Sure.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.000
What do ya think?

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.330
It's nice! I'll get this one.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.750
I knew it'd look perfect on ya.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:51.410
You have good taste in hats,
so how do you go so wrong with your clothes?

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.250
Shut it.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.700
If I were to pick out a jacket
to go with this hat...

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.620
That's super cute! Why don't you go with that?

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.750
Yeah. Now, let's see the price...

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.450
Twenty... thou?!

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:09.410
This one, too? And this?!

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.620
Whoa, that's expensive!

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:12.700
Shh!

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.200
Sorry.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:19.660
The hat is a normal price. I had no idea
the jacket would be that expensive...

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:23.410
Just get a Jacke! We can match.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.410
Nope.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.870
Not happening.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:26.870
Aw...

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.660
"Apparel"

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.250
I'll make it just barely.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.410
Did you find a good one?

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.700
Yeah, I was just thinking
how cute this logo was.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:55.080
Then you should get that one.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.750
But if I buy this,
I won't be able to buy a hat...

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.160
What should I do?

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:02.950
Whisper, whisper...

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.910
Whisper, whisper, whisper...

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.950
Hina! Just buy the jacket.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:09.790
You can get the hat another time!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.620
You might regret it if you don't buy it now.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.450
Y-You think so?

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.580
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.500
I'll take this one!

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:21.910
I've made up my mind!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.040
Thank you very much.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.620
Glad ya found one ya liked.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.870
Indeed.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.120
I'm going to wear this
to club starting tomorrow!

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.660
Well, don't you sound motivated.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.080
Let's catch some more big ones like flatheads!

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.830
I'd prefer to catch some
smaller ones if possible...

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:47.540
"Sankai Fishing Center"
Did you buy something, too, Natsumi?

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.500
Yeah, just a little something.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.750
Man, I sure wanted that chocolate parfait.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:56.330
How unfortunate.
And I was planning to treat you, too.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:58.450
Wait, really?

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:06.160
Thank you all for coming with me today.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.540
Thanks to you, I was able to find a cute jacket.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.620
Hey, don't sweat it. It was nothing.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.830
More importantly...

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.000
Here you go, Hina.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.790
Huh? What is this?

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:19.950
Open it!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.160
This is...

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.700
It's a present from the three of us!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.450
Huh? What?!

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.160
Huh? But why though?

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.540
Um... to congratulate you moving here?
Just take it.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.830
But I feel bad...

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.410
It's no biggie.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.330
Stop worryin' so much and just take it.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.580
Please.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.700
I-In that case...

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.870
President Kuroiwa, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>...
Thank you very much.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:55.080
Oh, come on now. This was all Natsumi's idea.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.290
Make sure ya thank her, too.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.200
Huh?!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:02.040
Th-Thanks... I'll take good care of it...

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:06.950
N-Not sure why you said it like that,
but sure. I hope you like it.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.660
I've never had this happen before.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.000
Anyway, it's not like

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.750
I'm trying to make it harder for you
to leave the club or anything.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.540
Don't worry and enjoy it.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.450
Is that why ya bought it?

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.620
Hey, look, Hina!
The sun's setting. It's so pretty...

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.540
Just so ya know, Tsurugi,
I just wanted to give ya a present.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.750
Me, too...

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.160
Natsumi!

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:46.330
I mean... I really did want
to give you a pres-- Ow!

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.660
Ugh, forget you!

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:54.910
"Report 04"
"'Eging'"
"Diary of Our Days at the Breakwater"

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:58.660
Ta-dah!

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.080
I'm wearing these for club today.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.790
You're all pumped up.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:08.750
Well, if ya ever change yer mind,
I'll let ya borrow my Jacke.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.120
Nah, I'm okay...

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.700
By the way, where's Ohno-<i>senpai</i>?

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.080
I think she had a student council meeting today.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:19.830
She should be headin' over here any minute.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.910
Then let's get ready for when she gets here.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.120
Sure.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.950
So, what are we fishing today?

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.450
Today...

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.500
"Spring Means Squid"
...we're fishin' for these!

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.370
"Squid"

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.620
Squid?

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.290
You can fish for squid from the breakwater?

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.950
Ya sure can.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.620
In the spring, they come to lay eggs
in seaweed in the shoals.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.200
That's when we're gonna strike.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.830
It's pretty common when you're
fishing at the breakwater.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:51.620
Not to mention, squid are delicious.
Especially freshly caught squid sashimi.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.290
Huh?!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.120
Especially when ya catch them yerself.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.080
Freshly caught squid sashimi.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.080
I want to eat some so bad!

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.160
I wonder if you can catch any, Hina.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.120
All right! I'm definitely going to catch some!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.370
First, we need to set up our rig.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:23.830
Ooh, what is that? It almost looks
like a very colorful... shrimp?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:27.500
Yup. It's a shrimp jig called "<i>Egi</i>."

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.750
So "<i>ebi</i>" like shrimp?

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:30.580
No, <i>Egi</i>.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:34.000
Ya move them like this to lure the squid.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.750
When ya fish for squid with these,
it's called "Eging."

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.750
Here ya go.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.200
So it's a little shrimpy called <i>Egi</i>.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:46.750
The more I look at it, the more it
looks like patchwork and looks cute.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.790
It's... cute?

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.040
It's not like I understand that side of Hina.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:56.950
Well, whatever.
I'll show ya how to set up the rig.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:59.120
First, the line.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:00.540
This is a PE line.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.290
It's almost like the thread
we use in handicrafts.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.910
Now we're gonna add a shock leader to the line.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.870
Shock le...?

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.620
This one seems more like vinyl.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.450
By tying together two lines
with different consistencies

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.660
the <i>Egi</i>s become easier to control,

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.950
and even if they get caught on some rocks,
yer line won't break easily.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.700
Wow...

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.870
Natsumi, tie the knot, will ya?

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:30.000
Knot?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.290
Wait, why me?

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.910
Do it yourself, Sis.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:38.750
How many times do I have to tell ya
to call me "President" out here?

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.620
Okay, I give up!

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.910
It's called a clinch knot.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.000
Oh.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.040
So this is called a knot, too.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.250
Pretty much.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.950
So... Could ya tie another one for me?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.700
Tie your own!

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.750
How about ya do it for me, Tsurugi?

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.580
You know it's not that easy
to do just after seeing it once!

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:08.330
I think I'll give it a try.
I mean, even Natsumi can do it.

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:10.330
Hina...

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:16.450
This actually looks better than Natsumi's.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:21.200
Next, ya just put on yer snap and then yer <i>Egi</i>.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.620
And done.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.500
Sorry I'm late.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.870
Good work.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.250
Hello.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.910
Perfect timing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:31.950
Well, let's get goin'.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.410
Yeah!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.410
♬ Spring squid! Spring squid! ♬

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.540
♬ Freshly caught squid sashimi! ♬

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.120
♬ Yummy sashimi! ♬

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.700
--The heck kind of song is that?
--♬ Spring squid! ♬

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.160
--It sounds fun.
--♬ Squid sashimi! ♬

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.950
--And... Hina, you look cute in your jacket.
--♬ Sashimi! I can't wait! ♬

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.540
Thank you.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:06.450
All right. I'll show you how to catch them!

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.830
Wait, you're showing me?

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:14.290
How rude! I've been fishing since
I was a little kid, just so you know!

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:15.750
Just you watch!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:21.040
First, you randomly cast your line
where you think some squid will be!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.540
You're already saying "randomly."

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:29.160
Then wait a little while for the <i>Egi </i>to sink.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.250
How long should I wait?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:32.910
Um... You'll figure it out.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.620
Are you really trying to teach me?

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.410
Okay, it reached the bottom.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:41.120
Now, to make the squid realize the <i>Egi</i>'s there,

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.750
you pull up your line twice real big.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.040
Then you let your <i>Egi </i>sink...

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:51.120
Once it's gotten close to the bottom,
you fwip it up like that.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.500
You want them to think the <i>Egi</i>'s alive.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.540
Then you let it sink again.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.160
Rinse and repeat.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:01.750
You almost seem like you know what
you're talking about. You almost seem cool.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.540
Was the "almost" necessary?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.410
More importantly, the key is to let it sink.

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:09.250
Squid tend to grab on when it's sinking--

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.120
I got one suddenly!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:16.790
Yeah... Looks like ya just
got snagged on somethin'.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.330
I can't believe I lost one
already on the first try.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:21.830
Well? Do you get how to fish for them now?

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:25.620
Yeah, I'll be careful not to snag my line.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:29.910
Here. I only have two for each of ya,
so be careful with them.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.000
Meaning this is yer last one, Natsumi.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.080
I shall be careful, kind lady.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:39.750
All right. I'm gonna get one before Natsumi!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:43.330
And I'm not gonna lose to your flimsy casting!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:47.790
Hiyah!

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.000
There!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.290
We're not catching any at all.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.620
Maybe there aren't any squid.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.950
It's quite rare that none
of us are catching any.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.700
Well, there're days like this, too.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:36.580
Guess we can call it for the day.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.040
Hey, a squid!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.250
Hina, cast your <i>Egi </i>and lure it in.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.370
O-Okay!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:44.540
I'll go, too!

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.410
Wait, why'd it ignore it?

00:18:56.120 --> 00:19:01.200
It's no use. We're just not convincing enough.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.790
That's a big one.

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:04.910
Don't just stand there. Catch it!

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.950
Ohno.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.330
You're so cool, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.370
Look at those moves!

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:33.120
She got it! Hina, let's get the net ready!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.370
S-Sure!

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.370
Get the net out there!

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.700
Okay, we got it!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.950
You're amazing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.870
That's an oval squid... and a big one.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.910
So it's called an oval squid?

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:58.660
Hey, it came in handy already.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:01.910
It's not funny!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.330
Don't worry.

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:06.040
It's water repellent, so it'll come off
as soon as you wash it.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.040
All right. Let's hurry up and finish it off.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:12.330
We need to eat it while it's still delicious.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.700
Finish it off?

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:16.830
Remember? Like when ya
finished off that flathead.

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:21.120
We kill it quick to keep its freshness.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.870
Oh... I guess that's what you meant.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.500
Whoa, it turned all see-through!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:40.080
And then with the lower half,
you turn it towards their arms and...

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:44.700
Wow, I sort of feel bad
for the squid, but this is neat.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.620
Right? I think so, too.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.790
Right, let's start heading back
towards the club room.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:51.700
Okay.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.500
Yay, squid sashimi!

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:59.660
Wow! It turned into sashimi in an instant.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.580
You're so amazing, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:04.450
Let's eat, already!

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:08.620
Now, hang on.
The one who caught it gets first dibs.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.040
Oh, okay. Thank you.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.660
It's so good.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.580
Right, then. Now let's all dig in.

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:22.540
Let's eat!

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:26.330
It's so yummy!

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.410
I've never had squid this yummy!

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:30.500
Right?

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:31.200
Yeah!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.290
But--

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.290
It's even better when you catch it yourself...

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.000
...right?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.040
Yeah!

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.700
All right! I'm definitely
catching one next time!

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.620
Let's catch lots so we can
have a full course of just squid!

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:44.750
Yeah!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:47.830
The sashimi is delicious,
but deep-fried would be great, too.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.700
How about some squid rice, too?

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:51.700
It's delicious in pasta, too.

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.040
Ooh!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:58.040
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.040 --> 00:21:59.500
Wear hats when fishing.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.950
It's important to wear one

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:02.500
to avoid heat stroke.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.540
By Hina.
